    "# Quiz: Introduction to clustering\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-1-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>A real-life example of clustering would be</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Setting the dinner table</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Clustering means sorting things into groups, like sorting laundry into each family member's clothes.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Sorting the laundry</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Sorting a pile of laundry into each family member's clothes is a real-life example of clustering.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Grocery shopping</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A real-life example of clustering is sorting a pile of laundry into each family member's clothes.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-1-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Clustering techniques can be used in these industries</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>banking</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Banking is one, but clustering is also used in e-commerce.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>e-commerce</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. E-commerce is one, but clustering is also used in banking.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>both of these</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Clustering shows up in banking, e-commerce and other business settings.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-1-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Clustering is a type of:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>supervised learning</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Clustering works on unlabeled data, so it is unsupervised, not supervised.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>unsupervised learning</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Clustering is unsupervised learning. It finds groups in data that has no labels.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>reinforcement learning</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Clustering is unsupervised learning that sorts unlabeled data into groups.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
