   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-1-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Euclidean geometry is arranged along</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>planes</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Euclidean geometry is 'flat' geometry, and parts of it are taught as 'plane' geometry.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>curves</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Distances measured along a curve are non-Euclidean, or 'non-flat'. Euclidean geometry is flat.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>spheres</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Euclidean geometry is 'flat' geometry. Parts of it are taught as 'plane' geometry.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-1-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>The density of your clustering data is related to its</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>noise</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. In density-based clustering, points are grouped by how crowded they are. Points far from the group count as noise.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>depth</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Density is about how crowded the points are. Points far from the crowded groups count as noise.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>validity</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Density is about how crowded the points are, and points far from the group count as noise.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-1-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>The best-known clustering algorithm is</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>k-means</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. K-means is a popular centroid clustering method. It groups data around k center points.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>k-middle</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The popular algorithm is k-means. Its center is found from the nearest mean, which gives it its name.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>k-mart</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The popular clustering algorithm is k-means. It is named for the mean that sets each cluster's center.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
